message.content:
Bug on Today tab: Alert.alert calls don't fire on web (React Native Web silently no-ops them).

Fix: replace both Alert.alert calls with a cross-platform approach:
- If Platform.OS === 'web': use window.alert(message)
- Otherwise: use Alert.alert(title, message)

Create a small helper at the top of today.tsx:

const showAlert = (title: string, message: string) => {
  if (Platform.OS === 'web') {
    window.alert(`${title}\n\n${message}`)
  } else {
    Alert.alert(title, message, [{ text: 'OK' }])
  }
}

Use showAlert for both:
1. "Practice this" button → showAlert('Practice this challenge', 'Coming soon — for now, get counsel on it instead.')
2. Locked past challenge cards → showAlert('Locked', "Past challenges unlock with a daily streak. Today's is ready now.")

Import Platform from react-native if not already imported. Apply.

